Sawblade phase 5.1a patch against sevagh/demucs.cpp f1206e9adeea103aef4a636b9e62297cf1f8e34e (MIT).
Applied by spikes/separator/CMakeLists.txt via patches/apply_patch.cmake. Regenerate with `git diff` in a checkout.

  model_apply.cpp  - shift fixed at 0: no rand(), no shift padding (4/6-source path and V3 path)
                   - Python-compatible context padding: every segment, including the short last one, is
                     filled with the real neighbouring audio (demucs.apply.TensorChunk.padded semantics),
                     zeros only beyond the track ends; output trimmed with center_trim (delta // 2)
                   - cancel flag: demucs_inference(model, audio, cb, const std::atomic<bool>* cancel = nullptr),
                     polled between segments; cancelled => returns an EMPTY tensor (dimension(0) == 0)
                   - FTZ/DAZ (x86 MXCSR bits 15 and 6, ARM FPCR.FZ) on the calling thread and on every
                     OpenMP worker of the team that Eigen/OpenBLAS GEMMs use; restored on return
                   - no std::cout
  model_load.cpp   - no stdout/stderr; load_demucs_model reports failure only through its return value
  layers.cpp, crosstransformer.cpp - invariant violations abort() instead of printing
  model.hpp        - new demucs_inference signature (default argument keeps old callers compiling)

